Domain layout for the Library world kit.

Each domain is a folder under /domains/<name>/ with three subfolders:

  items/   portable objects from the wand `create` verb
  rooms/   rooms from the wand `room` verb
  npcs/    living NPCs from the wand `npc` verb

Set the active domain with the wand: `domain <name>`. `create`,
`room`, `npc`, `edit`, and `exit` then write under that domain.
`domain` with no argument reports the current domain. `domain none`
clears it.

With no domain set, those verbs still write the legacy path
/data/created/<name>.c.

Inheritables used by generated files are named in worldkit.h
(ITEM_INH, ROOM_INH, NPC_INH).

domains/example/ is an empty stub so the tree is present at boot.
It holds no content.
